# The pinned Markdown To agent skill.
#
# SKILL.md and examples/*.md in this directory are a VERBATIM COPY of
# skills/markdownto/ from the markdownto repository at the commit below. They
# are never edited here: the skill is spec-agnostic by design — it teaches an
# agent to DISCOVER the spec family (`mdto spec`, https://markdownto.ai/llms.txt)
# rather than reciting a closed roster — so a pinned copy stays correct as the
# family grows, and an upgrade is a deliberate, reviewable commit.
#
# The four examples/ files are the byte-normative templates the markdownto
# conformance suite validates. Nothing in this repo can validate them (that
# needs the mdto CLI), so the pin below IS the guarantee: these are those exact
# bytes.
#
# Re-vendoring (docs/internals/markdownto-skill.md has the full procedure):
#
#   1. cp -R <markdownto>/skills/markdownto/{SKILL.md,examples} <agentsfs>/skills/markdownto/
#   2. Update commit + every sha256 below
#      (git -C <markdownto> rev-parse HEAD;
#       shasum -a 256 skills/markdownto/SKILL.md skills/markdownto/examples/*.md)
#   3. go test ./internal/skills/ ./internal/hub/ -run MarkdownTo
#      (the manifest is asserted against the embedded bytes, so a stale line
#      here fails the build, not an agent's session)
#
# Format: `key: value`, one per line; `#` comments and blank lines ignored.
# A `sha256 <path>` key pins one file, relative to this directory.

